cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SafeSpec in your research, please cite the following work."
title: "SafeSpec: Asynchronous Safety Probing for Speculative Decoding"
abstract: >
  SafeSpec is an open-source reference implementation of asynchronous
  safety probing for LLM speculative decoding.  A small, trainable safety
  probe (Qwen3Guard-Stream-0.6B + LoRA) is inserted into the draft/verify
  loop of a speculative decoder (Qwen3-0.6B draft + Qwen3-8B target) with
  three latency-hiding optimisations (torch.compile, dedicated CUDA stream,
  background-thread dispatch) so that the probe adds essentially zero
  user-perceived wall-time while contributing streaming prompt-injection
  detection at FNR < 2.5 %.
authors:
  - family-names: "SafeSpec Authors"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-05"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/hsj576/SafeSpec"
keywords:
  - speculative-decoding
  - safety-probe
  - prompt-injection-detection
  - LoRA
  - Qwen3Guard
